[candidate · 0:56] Let me size the beans first. Beans were 25% of a 42% COGS line, so about 10.5 points of revenue. Up 40% adds ~4.2 points. The other 31.5 points rose 37.5%, adding ~11.8 points. Total ~16 points — matches. But the split matters: beans are only about a quarter of the damage. Dairy, packaging and food are three-quarters.

